m=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured HashiCorp Raft Go module: consensus loops, replication, membership, log/snapshot interfaces and FSM completion. FSM application semantics and durable backend implementation are caller-selected; in-repository mechanisms remain in scope.',protocol_contexts=['Leader election term','Latest and committed configurations','Per-tenure commitment and per-peer replication','Snapshot/log prefix','VerifyLeader invocation'],external_interfaces=['Transport','LogStore','StableStore','SnapshotStore','FSM','Apply and VerifyLeader'],ownership=['Main loop owns normal protocol/configuration processing; replication, FSM and snapshot routines have distinct asynchronous duties.','NetworkTransport can invoke restricted zero-data heartbeat callbacks independently.'],selection_injection=['NewRaft accepts stores, FSM and Transport; network and in-memory transports are provided in repository.'],source_ids=['src-startup','src-transport','src-fastpath'],unknowns=['Backend-specific crash atomicity and alternate transport ordering remain outside this initial reading.']),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=facts,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='Raft.appendEntries commit bound',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-append','b-replicate'],reason='Can normal backtracking or a legal overlap ever deliver a batch ending before a divergent local suffix while advertising a greater commit index?',source_ids=['src-append-consumer','src-replication-retry','src-request-producer'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.verifyLeader participant eligibility',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-verify','b-membership'],reason='Verification threshold counts voters but notification registration spans all replication peers. Determine applicable support responsibility and legal consequence.',source_ids=['src-verify-start','src-verify-notify','src-lease','src-config-types'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.persistVote partial storage failure',disposition='deferred',reason='Separate vote term and candidate writes: determine permitted failure/restart behavior and prior candidate reuse.',source_ids=['src-persist-context'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='NetworkTransport heartbeat callback context',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-append','b-leader-context'],reason='Fast path excludes log/commit data but changes term/state concurrently with normal processing; overlapping ownership merits separate examination.',source_ids=['src-startup','src-fastpath','src-rpc-dispatch'],high_consequence=True)],core_overview=dict(status='usable',core_gaps=[],formation=path('A1: leader dispatch assigns term/index and persists logs before recording its match and notifying peer replicators. Per-peer requests carry previous prefix, bounded entries and commit index; success supplies stored-prefix support to a captured commitment object. Only configured voters count, and its majority index must reach the first entry of this leader term. The main loop consumes commit notification, marks configuration committed and queues logs. Followers validate term/previous prefix, truncate supplied conflicts and propagate leader commit accounting into their own queue. FSM execution and future completion occur later on the FSM goroutine. Snapshot transfer substitutes a persisted/restored prefix when logs are unavailable.',['b-dispatch','b-replicate','b-aggregate','b-append','b-application','b-recovery'],['f-match','f-commit']),context=path('A2: contact timeout triggers a eligible local voter campaign; pre-vote probes where supported, then electSelf persists a new term/self vote and asks configured voters through a campaign-local response channel. Vote receivers reject ineligible/stale or less-up-to-date candidates and preserve one vote per term. Majority grants install leader state. Higher-term requests, replication higher-term responses, loss of lease quorum and committed removal can end tenure. Transfer first catches up its target then requests an accelerated campaign. Startup restores term, snapshot and membership history but starts as follower.',['b-election','b-leader-context','b-membership','b-transfer','b-recovery','b-history'],['f-authority']),connection=path('Each tenure creates fresh commitment/replication objects, captures its term and sends a no-op; the current-term threshold constrains commitment of inherited history. Old RPC replies retain old campaign channels or commitment pointers, while follower term checks reject obsolete requests. Leader exit signals replication to stop and fails pending client/verify futures; it does not erase stored or already queued history. New authority is constrained by log freshness and recovered configuration. Configuration changes serialize after a current-term commit, then alter voter eligibility while retaining matching support for retained voters. Committed entries are separately consumed by the FSM, and a failed client future does not imply absence from later history. VerifyLeader is another authority consumer whose voter threshold and all-peer notifications have an unresolved eligibility relationship.',['b-election','b-leader-context','b-membership','b-replicate','b-aggregate','b-application','b-client','b-verify'],['f-authority','f-match','f-commit','f-verify-support']),open_details=['Verification participant eligibility and stale-read consequence under actual lease/election timing.','Follower commit bound reachability under backtracking and overlapping work.','Partial stable-store failures; retained snapshot suffixes; heartbeat/main-loop context overlap; transfer cancellation races.'],rationale='Representative formation, authority transitions, old-work ownership, persistent recovery and application completion have been traced. Local anomalies and deeper variants remain open; usability is a basis for investigation, not a correctness or coverage claim.'))
